# End-to-end EMULATOR test for the Duet3 6HC (SAME70Q20B) in
# DETERMINISTIC TICK MODE. Boots klipper firmware under Renode against
# the duet3-6hc pin map, completes klippy identify + clocksync, brings
# up the full MCU config (4 TMC5160s on a shared SPI daisy-chain, 2
# software-PWM heaters, fans, endstops, adc_scaled thermistors), reads
# the thermistors through adc_scaled (vref/vssa-compensated) on the
# SAME70 AFEC, round-trips the four TMC5160 register files over the SPI
# chain, and exercises interactive gcode (M114/M105) against real
# firmware.
#
# This is the SAME70 sibling of duet2_maestro (SAM4S) / skr_mini_e3_v2
# (STM32F103) / skr_pico (RP2040). What it adds: TMC5160 over a SPI
# DAISY-CHAIN (chain_length 6) on usart1, driven by the renode_hooks
# TMC SPI chain responder (CPU-PC hook on spidev_transfer - Renode
# models no USART-in-SPI-mode peripheral, so the responder reads MOSI
# from the firmware buffer, synthesises the chain MISO response with a
# one-transaction-delay-per-slot model, and PC-skips the real hardware
# transfer). DUMP_TMC reads back the live register file for chain
# positions 1 (stepper_x) and 4 (extruder), proving the chain read path.
#
# The real Duet3 6HC is USB+CAN only. This test runs the serial-mode build
# (same70q20b.dict, host link UART2 on PD25/PD26) because the pin map it
# exercises is host-link independent; its USB-CDC sibling duet3_6hc_usb.test
# drives the identical config over the real USB-CDC host link
# (same70q20b-usb.dict) now that the renode ARM tick byte-shuttle survives
# identify (klippy/serialhdl.py honors the bounded need_prompt quantum for
# the renode pty). Free-run SAME70 clocksync drifts badly under a multi-SPI
# config and drops the connection mid-init, so the test runs in tick mode
# (clocksync converges flat at 300 MHz). Motion-free, as with the other
# per-printer tests.
DICTIONARY same70q20b.dict
CONFIG duet3_6hc.cfg
EMULATOR duet3_6hc.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

M114
M105
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_x
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=extruder

EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
# DUMP_TMC dumped both ends of the chain (pos 1 / pos 4); IOIN
# version=0x30 proves the SPI chain read path round-tripped.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC stepper_x"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC extruder"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "version=0x30"
# adc_scaled requires (vref - vssa) != 0; without the AFEC stub feeding
# the reference channels both read 0 and klippy raises ZeroDivisionError.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ZeroDivisionError"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to write tmc spi"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to read tmc spi"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ADC out of range"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
